========================================================================
  PART 7: SIZE FORMULAS — COLLECTING THE PATTERN
========================================================================


  PoS class sizes:
    n=5: |PoS(5)| = 280
    n=6: |PoS(6)| = 8640

  Decomposition:
    n=5: Case1 = 40, Case2 = 240. Total = 280.
    n=6: Case1 = 720, Case2 = 7920. Total = 8640.

  PATTERNS:
    n=5: 280 = 5 × 4 × 14 = 20 × 14
    n=6: 8640 = 6 × 5 × 288

    Actually: 280 = C(5,1) × C(4,1) × 14
    And 14 = number of tournaments per (sink,source) pair

    Can we express 14 in terms of n?
    At n=5: 14 tournaments per pair = 2 (Case 1) + 12 (Case 2) = 14
    At n=6: 24.0 (Case 1 per pair) + 264.0 (Case 2 per pair) per pair

  At n=5: 20 pairs × 14 per pair = 280
  At n=6: 30 pairs × (24 + 264) per pair = 8640

  Case 1 per pair: # middle tournaments with 'right' internal scores
    n=5: 2 (= #{regular C₃} on 3 vertices)
    n=6: 24 (= #{specific tournaments on 4 vertices})

